WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.334
Exclusive report on a

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.236
federal criminal investigation

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:05.372
into former President Donald Trump.

00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:07.007
Attorneys for the former president

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:08.108
unable now

00:00:08.108 --> 00:00:10.076
to locate a classified document

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:11.678
that he referenced on an audiotape

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:13.880
now in possession of prosecutors.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.949
CNN's Kaitlan Collins is on the team

00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:16.883
that broke this story.

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:18.351
She's joining us now with the latest.

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:19.719
Caitlin, take us through what we know

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:20.653
so what happened.

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:21.187
Here is

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:21.855
Maria Martin,

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:23.523
this press aide to former

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:24.324
President Trump,

00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:25.191
who was in the White House

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:26.226
and now has followed him to Mar

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:27.127
a Lago, went

00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:27.994
and testified

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:29.729
as many people who are in that orbit,

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:31.765
these days have gone before MS.

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:32.732
investigators.

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:34.601
And she was in there in mid-March.

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:35.201
And we're told

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:37.203
it was very shortly after she left

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:38.671
that grand jury testimony.

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.440
The prosecutor sent a subpoena

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.775
to the former president

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:42.642
saying that they wanted

00:00:42.642 --> 00:00:45.078
any and all documents related to Iran.

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:46.212
And General Mark Milley,

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:46.980
the chairman of the Joint

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:47.714
Chiefs of Staff,

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:49.349
that Trump is referencing

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:50.417
on that audio recording

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:52.519
that we reported on on Wednesday.

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:53.186
And basically,

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:54.187
what I was told

00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:55.455
that they were specifically seeking

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:56.289
was the document

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:58.158
that Trump is referencing on that tape.

00:00:58.158 --> 00:01:00.126
Prosecutors made clear to Trump's

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:01.561
legal team that they wanted

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:02.796
that document.

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:03.396
Trump's team,

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:04.831
though, was unable to find it.

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:06.332
They did produce some materials,

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:07.767
we were told, in response

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:09.536
to this subpoena that they got

00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:10.270
they could not find

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:11.104
that document, though.

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:11.871
That is at the heart

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:13.139
of what Trump was referencing.

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:14.174
So it's raised

00:01:14.174 --> 00:01:14.941
a lot of questions

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:16.476
of where that document is.

00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:18.611
I asked Trump's attorney the other day

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:19.612
if it had been sent back

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:20.513
to the National Archives,

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:21.481
what happened to it.

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:22.582
He declined to answer.

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:24.117
He also didn't say whether or not Trump

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:25.085
had declassified.

00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:26.953
It is an argument they've been making.

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:28.388
So this is just raised questions

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:30.623
about this episode, which we know.

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:31.191
Jack Smith,

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:32.826
the special counsel, is very focused on.

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:32.992
I mean,

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:34.260
they even brought General Mark Milley

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.729
in to talk to him about this episode

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:38.264
because Trump was referencing him

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:40.233
when he was on that audio recording

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:42.001
discussing classified information.

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:43.403
All right, Caitlin, stay with us.

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:44.370
I want to bring in more

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.106
of our legal experts.

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:47.807
Elliot Williams, to you.

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:48.842
It is possible

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:50.677
that the Justice Department

00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:53.346
recovered this document some other way.

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.048
How much does this document

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:56.416
actually matter when,

00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:58.184
according to Caitlin's reporting,

00:01:58.184 --> 00:01:59.085
the prosecutors do

00:01:59.085 --> 00:02:01.254
have this audio tape of President Trump,

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:02.989
Trump himself talking about it?

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:03.690
Look, it doesn't

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:04.591
it doesn't write

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:07.160
the crime is retention of material

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:08.962
that is related to the national defense.

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:09.462
Now that

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:10.163
the crime doesn't say

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:11.898
that, you need to have the document there

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:13.433
in order to prosecute the person for it,

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:14.367
you just have to establish

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:17.003
the document went missing and someone

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:18.037
had it improperly.

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:19.339
Or retained it improperly.

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:19.772
Now, look,

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:20.974
this would be novel

00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:22.509
to charge someone with a crime

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:24.277
for a document

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:25.278
that they're not in possession of.

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:26.379
But but a few things.

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:27.046
Number one,

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:28.314
the Defense Department likely

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:29.382
has a copy of it.

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:30.049
Number two,

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:30.850
you could get people

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.919
who made the document or are aware of it

00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:34.621
to testify about where it was

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:35.822
and where it went until the point

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:37.023
at which it went missing.

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:38.424
So you can get around it a little bit

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:40.393
and they can find a way

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:41.494
to charge someone with a crime.

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:42.662
But it might just

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:43.930
require a little bit of creativity

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:44.597
from prosecutors.

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:45.398
So the former president

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:47.300
has been asked about this

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:48.001
missing document.

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:50.904
Here's what he had to say.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.038
No, I don't know anything about it.

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:53.406
All I know is this.

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:55.074
Everything I did was right.

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:56.876
We have the Presidential Records Act,

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:58.645
which I abided by 100%.

00:02:58.645 --> 00:02:59.212
I have the right

00:02:59.212 --> 00:03:00.813
to declassify as president

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:01.881
because I have Secret Service

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:02.715
all over the place.

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:05.418
Mar a Lago is a fort

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:07.086
chain. Mar a Lago is a fort.

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:07.954
He's got Secret Service

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:09.355
all over the place.

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:11.424
Does that stand up in any way?

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:13.059
Well, that's kind of irrelevant

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:13.293
as to

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:15.595
whether he properly secured the document.

00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:17.931
He allegedly should not have retained,

00:03:17.931 --> 00:03:18.631
which he claims.

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.567
If I did have it, it was declassified.

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:22.035
That's kind of the problem for him.

00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:23.403
He's all over the place

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:25.305
trying to cover all his bases.

00:03:25.305 --> 00:03:27.440
The audiotape, as well as the subpoena

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:28.575
puts him in his legal team,

00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:29.976
the difficult spot.

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:31.344
He's going to have to make

00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:32.912
the Hobson's choice of saying either

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:34.147
I had this and was fine

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:35.415
for me to have it or

00:03:35.415 --> 00:03:36.249
what are you talking about?

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:37.884
I was just blabbing on that tape.

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:39.552
But to do that,

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:41.988
he probably would have to testify.

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:43.623
And that's problematic for him

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:45.458
because you don't want him to testify.

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:47.060
He his lawyers could make that argument

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:47.794
if they got the court.

00:03:47.794 --> 00:03:48.428
There's no proof

00:03:48.428 --> 00:03:49.562
he really had that document.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:50.897
He was just blowing hot air

00:03:50.897 --> 00:03:51.998
as he likes to do.

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:54.367
But to make it really convincing,

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:55.101
the jury would

00:03:55.101 --> 00:03:56.002
probably want to hear from them.

00:03:56.002 --> 00:03:57.136
So that's a problem.

00:03:57.136 --> 00:04:00.073
And in terms of the timing of Jack Smith,

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:03.142
the special counsel's investigation,

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:05.745
Elliot, where do you think we are

00:04:05.745 --> 00:04:07.714
in terms of potential indictments?

00:04:07.714 --> 00:04:09.182
There was one former

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:11.017
prosecutor predicting that indictment

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:13.186
could come within days.

00:04:13.186 --> 00:04:14.787
Well, look, I

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:15.755
you know, it's hard to predict

00:04:15.755 --> 00:04:16.923
when things will happen.

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:18.024
What I will say

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:18.891
is that we don't know what

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:20.093
the Justice Department has.

00:04:20.093 --> 00:04:21.294
That's not public.

00:04:21.294 --> 00:04:21.794
What is

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:23.630
public is a growing body

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:24.731
of statements from the former

00:04:24.731 --> 00:04:25.932
president

00:04:25.965 --> 00:04:27.433
leaks and other information

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:29.068
that have been reported

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:30.470
that seem to suggest

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:31.104
that at least

00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:32.739
someone ought to be charged

00:04:32.739 --> 00:04:33.906
with a crime in some way,

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:35.441
whether it's obstruction of justice

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:38.244
retention or removal of

00:04:38.411 --> 00:04:39.712
sensitive information,

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:40.680
they could be charged.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:41.281
And that's just based on

00:04:41.281 --> 00:04:42.215
what's publicly available.

00:04:42.215 --> 00:04:43.583
It's hard to even know what else

00:04:43.583 --> 00:04:44.751
the Justice Department is sitting on.

00:04:44.751 --> 00:04:45.618
So it could be imminent,

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:47.053
but we just don't know.

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:48.087
Is the Trump team

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:49.355
saying anything about what they think

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:51.057
the timeframe might be?

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:52.659
They have maintained that

00:04:52.659 --> 00:04:53.393
they don't believe

00:04:53.393 --> 00:04:54.327
there's a threat to him,

00:04:54.327 --> 00:04:54.961
that they don't think

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:56.596
he'll be indicted in this case.

00:04:56.596 --> 00:04:57.530
His former attorney,

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:58.865
who's no longer on the legal team, left

00:04:58.865 --> 00:05:00.500
about two weeks ago,

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:01.067
downplayed

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:02.201
the idea that he would be indicted

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:03.002
the other day.

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:04.570
But behind the scenes,

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:05.605
based on our reporting,

00:05:05.605 --> 00:05:07.440
what we have heard from people is

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.409
the tone has shifted since this

00:05:09.409 --> 00:05:11.311
since we reported this on Wednesday.

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:13.112
I think they think the legal significance

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:13.780
of this,

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:15.281
they realize how grave it is

00:05:15.281 --> 00:05:16.282
and that it could potentially

00:05:16.282 --> 00:05:17.083
be a game changer

00:05:17.083 --> 00:05:19.052
when it comes to this investigation.

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:20.286
They had been pretty confident.

00:05:20.286 --> 00:05:21.721
They were almost joyous

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:23.022
when the documents

00:05:23.022 --> 00:05:24.324
were found at Pence's home.

00:05:24.324 --> 00:05:25.458
And the Biden documents

00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:26.225
situation happened.

00:05:26.225 --> 00:05:28.161
Very different situations, of course,

00:05:28.161 --> 00:05:29.295
but they were almost joyous all that

00:05:29.295 --> 00:05:31.097
because they thought it was essentially

00:05:31.097 --> 00:05:31.698
a guarantee

00:05:31.698 --> 00:05:32.231
that nothing

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:33.599
would happen to their client.

00:05:33.599 --> 00:05:34.934
I think the people around the former

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:36.002
president are very worried

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:37.070
now that they know

00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:38.438
Jack Smith has this audio.

00:05:38.438 --> 00:05:40.106
They've known about this since March,

00:05:40.106 --> 00:05:40.640
by the way.

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:42.275
They've been looking for this document.

00:05:42.275 --> 00:05:43.776
That was when they got the subpoena

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:45.044
They realize the legal peril

00:05:45.044 --> 00:05:45.945
that he's facing right now.

00:05:45.945 --> 00:05:47.313
You mentioned how joyous they were

00:05:47.313 --> 00:05:48.748
when more classified documents

00:05:48.748 --> 00:05:49.182
were found

00:05:49.182 --> 00:05:51.150
at President Biden's

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:53.252
residences and offices.

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:54.053
The former president,

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:55.321
Mike Pence's home as well.

00:05:55.321 --> 00:05:57.423
But Evan, you've got new reporting.

00:05:57.423 --> 00:05:59.192
Mike Pence has been cleared.

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:00.193
He has been cleared.

00:06:00.193 --> 00:06:01.160
He got a letter.

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:03.162
His team got a letter yesterday.

00:06:03.162 --> 00:06:03.629
That says

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:04.764
that the Justice Department,

00:06:04.764 --> 00:06:05.565
the National Security

00:06:05.565 --> 00:06:07.500
Division, have been investigating

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:08.534
this, a dozen

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:10.236
or so documents that were found.

00:06:10.236 --> 00:06:11.070
And they've decided that

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:12.872
there are no charges to be brought

00:06:12.872 --> 00:06:14.941
This obviously takes us back to January

00:06:14.941 --> 00:06:16.376
when they added

00:06:16.376 --> 00:06:17.410
an abundance of caution,

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:19.212
went looking for documents, partly

00:06:19.212 --> 00:06:20.713
because of what had happened

00:06:20.713 --> 00:06:23.182
with the former president, Donald Trump,

00:06:23.182 --> 00:06:25.485
who had a special counsel appointed

00:06:26.052 --> 00:06:26.586
as a result

00:06:26.586 --> 00:06:28.187
of having declared that he was

00:06:28.187 --> 00:06:29.088
running for president.

00:06:30.089 --> 00:06:30.656
Merrick Garland

00:06:30.656 --> 00:06:31.924
also appointed a special counsel

00:06:31.924 --> 00:06:33.860
to look at the documents

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:35.895
related to to President Biden.

00:06:36.095 --> 00:06:36.896
And so the question

00:06:36.896 --> 00:06:39.665
has been hanging over this review

00:06:39.899 --> 00:06:40.733
that has been ongoing,

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:41.567
this investigation,

00:06:41.567 --> 00:06:43.536
whether Mike Pence would also end up

00:06:43.536 --> 00:06:45.037
having a special counsel,

00:06:45.037 --> 00:06:46.372
because as we know,

00:06:46.372 --> 00:06:47.240
we're days away

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:48.708
from a likely announcement

00:06:48.708 --> 00:06:49.742
from the vice president,

00:06:49.742 --> 00:06:50.209
the former vice

00:06:50.209 --> 00:06:50.877
president saying

00:06:50.877 --> 00:06:52.478
that he is running for president.

00:06:52.478 --> 00:06:54.981
So this clears the decks for him.

00:06:54.981 --> 00:06:57.116
And look, again, as Caitlin pointed out,

00:06:58.217 --> 00:06:59.986
the circumstances are so different.

00:06:59.986 --> 00:07:00.253
Right.

00:07:00.253 --> 00:07:01.921
Mike Pence finds these documents

00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:03.389
Turns him over to

00:07:03.389 --> 00:07:06.092
to the National Archives and the FBI

00:07:06.092 --> 00:07:07.326
cooperates, fully

00:07:07.326 --> 00:07:08.761
allows for searches to come

00:07:08.761 --> 00:07:10.830
in, does not publicly claim

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:12.298
that that these documents

00:07:12.298 --> 00:07:12.932
are his

00:07:12.932 --> 00:07:14.167
completely different way

00:07:14.167 --> 00:07:14.867
of handling this.

00:07:14.867 --> 00:07:16.602
And you can see how quickly,

00:07:16.602 --> 00:07:16.969
you know,

00:07:16.969 --> 00:07:17.670
the Justice Department

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:19.172
can work through a situation like this

00:07:19.172 --> 00:07:20.873
when you have this level of corruption.

00:07:20.873 --> 00:07:21.474
To add one

00:07:21.474 --> 00:07:22.408
point to that,

00:07:22.408 --> 00:07:23.676
Pence affirmatively

00:07:23.676 --> 00:07:25.578
went looking for documents.

00:07:25.578 --> 00:07:27.013
He brought in his lawyers

00:07:27.013 --> 00:07:28.781
to conduct a search of his property.

00:07:28.781 --> 00:07:30.550
It's not that it was just inadvertent.

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:31.417
And they found these things

00:07:31.417 --> 00:07:33.486
it's just a different class of conduct.

